  "configuration_id": "config_016",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only/singleprofile/pca_n2000 at 48.5% acc), evidence is extremely sparse. The most critical design question for a multimodal cellular profiling study is whether adding an image modality to the RNA signal provides meaningful gains. config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) is the minimal, direct extension of the baseline: it keeps the same RNA encoder and profile setting and introduces only the image modality with the simplest fusion (concat). This isolates the effect of multimodality. If it substantially exceeds 48.5%, we know image adds signal and should invest in exploring fusion strategies, image encoders, and multiprofile within the multimodal space. If it does not, we learn that the bottleneck lies elsewhere (e.g., RNA encoder quality or profile aggregation) and can redirect budget toward those levers. No other single experiment resolves as many downstream design decisions under the limited budget."
}

